<h1>BananaType Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="meta">Effective date: 28 September 2026 &middot; Last updated: 28 September 2026 &middot; Developer: 4DVENTUREdev</p>

<div class="summary">
  <p><strong>The short version:</strong> BananaType is a keyboard, and what you type stays on your device. We don't collect it, store it, or send it anywhere. The only data collected in the app comes from Google AdMob, which shows the ads.</p>
</div>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>BananaType ("the app") is an Android keyboard for typing Chinese with Pinyin, with English definitions shown under each suggested word. It is published by 4DVENTUREdev ("we", "us"). If you have questions about this policy or your data, contact us at <a href="mailto:jasonjunchen07@gmail.com">jasonjunchen07@gmail.com</a>.</p>

<h2>What you type</h2>
<p>BananaType processes everything you type on your device only. We do not collect, record, log, store on a server, or transmit the text you type, the words you select, your passwords, or anything else entered with the keyboard. The dictionaries and word lists that power suggestions and definitions are bundled inside the app and work on your device.</p>
<p>The app does not ask for permission to access your contacts, location, camera, microphone, photos, or files, and it does not require an account. It uses internet access only to load ads and to open links (such as the Donate button), and it uses Android's advertising ID so that Google AdMob can show ads.</p>
<p>When you enable any third-party keyboard, Android displays a standard warning that the keyboard may be able to collect the text you type. That is a generic system message shown for every keyboard. BananaType does not collect your text.</p>

<h2>Data collected by advertising</h2>
<p>The app shows banner ads on its settings screen using Google AdMob, a service provided by Google. AdMob is third-party code inside the app, and it collects data itself when it loads and shows an ad. This can include:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your device's advertising ID (a resettable identifier that you control).</li>
  <li>Your IP address, from which a rough location can be worked out.</li>
  <li>Device and app information, such as device model, operating system version, and app version.</li>
  <li>How you interact with ads, such as views and taps.</li>
  <li>Diagnostic information, such as crash and performance data.</li>
</ul>
<p>Google uses this data to serve and measure ads and to prevent fraud and abuse, as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>. We do not receive your personal data from AdMob, and we do not sell personal data.</p>
<p>Ads are shown only on the app's settings screen. No ads appear on the keyboard itself, and AdMob has no access to what you type.</p>

<h2>Your choices about ads</h2>
<ul>
  <li>If you are in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, the app shows a consent message (provided by Google's User Messaging Platform) asking whether you agree to Google using your data for ads. Ads are not requested until you have made a choice where the law requires it. You can change your choice at any time using the "Privacy settings" option on the app's settings screen.</li>
  <li>You can reset your advertising ID or opt out of ads personalization in your Android settings, usually under <em>Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads</em> (the exact path varies by device).</li>
  <li>You can stop all data collection by AdMob by uninstalling the app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
<p>Because we do not collect or hold your personal data, there is generally nothing for us to access, correct, or delete. Depending on where you live (for example the EEA, the UK, California, or other US states), you may have rights over data that is collected about you, including the right to opt out of personalised advertising, to access or delete your data, and to withdraw consent. For data collected by Google AdMob, you can exercise these rights through your Android ad settings, through your Google account, or through the consent option in the app. You can also contact us at the email below and we will help where we can. We do not sell personal data, and we do not use your data for purposes other than those described in this policy.</p>

<h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
<p>The app stores its own settings and preferences on your device, such as your keyboard options. This information stays on your device and is removed when you uninstall the app.</p>

<h2>Sharing your data</h2>
<p>We do not sell, rent, or share personal data with third parties. The only third party that collects data through the app is Google, through AdMob, as described above. We may disclose information if required by law, but since we do not hold your personal data, we expect there would be nothing to disclose.</p>

<h2>Links to other sites</h2>
<p>The app includes a Donate button that opens our page on Buy Me a Coffee in your browser. That site is run by a separate company and has its own privacy policy. Donating is optional, and we do not receive or store your payment details.</p>

<h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
<p>We do not hold any personal data about you, so there is nothing for us to retain or delete. The app has no accounts. Uninstalling the app removes everything it stores on your device. Data that Google holds through AdMob is governed by Google's policies, and you can manage it at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy">myaccount.google.com</a>.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>Because your typing never leaves your device, there is no typed data on our side to secure. Ad requests are handled by Google's SDK, which generally uses encrypted connections.</p>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>BananaType is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 where local law sets a higher age), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the app, contact us and we will help resolve it.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If we change how the app handles data, we will update this page and the effective date above. Significant changes will also be described in the app's Google Play listing.</p>

<h2>Open-source and third-party components</h2>
<p>BananaType is built on a licensed fork of the OpenHeInput keyboard and uses the CC-CEDICT dictionary and the jieba word-frequency data, each under its own license. Full attributions are in the app's "Open Source Licenses" screen and in the project's NOTICE file. None of these components collect data.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions or requests about privacy: <a href="mailto:jasonjunchen07@gmail.com">jasonjunchen07@gmail.com</a>.</p>

